admin-inbound-title = Inbound access
admin-inbound-help = Restrict trusted source IPs for the admin console and webmail separately. Both policies start disabled. These rules do not change trusted proxies, API scopes or outbound access.
admin-inbound-unscoped = This deployment-wide policy requires an administrator with unscoped security access.
admin-inbound-admin = Admin console and API
admin-inbound-admin-help = Includes sign-in and this editor. Existing administrator authentication does not bypass the network policy.
admin-inbound-webmail = Webmail and account APIs
admin-inbound-webmail-help = Covers mail, DAV, signed content, SSO, OIDC and API routes. Existing upgraded connections keep their handshake decision.
admin-inbound-enabled = Restrict this surface to the allowlist
admin-inbound-cidrs = Rescue IPs and CIDRs
admin-inbound-cidrs-help = One literal IP or CIDR per line, up to 128. At least one is required when enabled. Include a trusted source you can use for recovery.
admin-inbound-hostnames = Allowed DNS hostnames
admin-inbound-hostnames-help = One lowercase ASCII DNS name per line. Use IDNA ASCII for international names. No URLs, ports, wildcards, IP literals or trailing dots. Names grant only current resolved addresses.
admin-inbound-dns = DNS resolution limits
admin-inbound-dns-help = New, expired and failed names grant no access. Successful answers respect their DNS TTL and the configured cache cap. Requests never wait for DNS resolution.
admin-inbound-servers = Recursive DNS servers
admin-inbound-servers-help = Leave empty for system resolvers, or enter up to four IP:port sockets, one per line (for example 10.0.0.53:53 or [fd00::53]:53). Explicit servers replace system resolvers without public fallback. Resolver trust is your responsibility; independent DNSSEC validation is not claimed.
admin-inbound-dns-timeoutMs = Lookup timeout (milliseconds)
admin-inbound-dns-cacheSeconds = Maximum cache lifetime (seconds)
admin-inbound-dns-maxHosts = Maximum distinct hostnames
admin-inbound-dns-maxAddresses = Maximum addresses per hostname
admin-inbound-dns-concurrency = Concurrent lookups
admin-inbound-bounds = Allowed range: { $min }–{ $max }.
admin-inbound-lockout = This policy can immediately block your own access, including this editor. Confirm that the rescue IPs cover your actual source as determined by the configured trusted proxies. There is no automatic loopback or signed-in administrator bypass. Recovery from a lockout requires deployment-side restoration; ordinary sign-in cannot bypass it.
admin-inbound-confirm-title = Apply inbound access policy?
admin-inbound-confirm-word = APPLY
admin-inbound-save = Apply confirmed policy
admin-inbound-review = Review changes
admin-inbound-refresh = Refresh saved policy and DNS status
admin-inbound-reset = Reset draft to loaded policy
admin-inbound-saved = The server accepted the inbound access policy.
admin-inbound-conflict = The saved policy changed while you were editing. Reset the draft and refresh to load its current revision before editing again.
admin-inbound-no-revision = The server did not return a policy revision. Refresh before saving.
admin-inbound-status = Current DNS grants
admin-inbound-status-help = This is a snapshot from the last status refresh, not a countdown or a connectivity probe. Refresh to see current grants. An error may coexist with a still-valid prior answer until its original expiry.
admin-inbound-refreshing = A bounded DNS refresh is in progress.
admin-inbound-idle = No DNS refresh was running at the last status read.
admin-inbound-no-hosts = No hostnames are active in enabled policies.
admin-inbound-hostname = Hostname
admin-inbound-state = Access grant
admin-inbound-addresses = Usable addresses
admin-inbound-validity = Validity at last refresh
admin-inbound-error = DNS result code
admin-inbound-usable = Usable
admin-inbound-unavailable = No current grant
admin-inbound-seconds = { $seconds } seconds
admin-inbound-on = Enabled
admin-inbound-off = Disabled
admin-inbound-invalid-dns = DNS limits or resolver count are outside the permitted bounds.
admin-inbound-rescue-required = Each enabled surface requires at least one rescue IP or CIDR.
admin-inbound-too-many = The policy exceeds the configured hostname or literal-address limit.
admin-inbound-invalid-host = Use lowercase ASCII DNS names without URLs, ports, wildcards, IP literals or trailing dots.
